foreign  24 2022 the day everything changed for  Ukraine  through the chaos one thing was clear  months of military buildup  would be no Bluff this was a Russian  invasion  from Belarus Southern Russia and Crimea  troops tanks and aircraft poured across  borders  fleeing the Russian Blitzkrieg civilians  crowded train stations and highways  hundreds of thousands of women and  children headed abroad men had to stay  my heart's being torn apart  I'm sorry  it's tough when families are separated  it's very hard  Ukraine was fighting for its survival as  a Sovereign Nation volunteers joined the  army and territorial defense groups  one of those who picked up a gun was  ihor  he helped defend earpin a key of suburb  that saw Fierce fighting  he who described to me what it had been  like  I had no fear I don't know why we were  all determined not to give up our land  we understood our weapons were weak  against their armor but we had  motivation  because of fierce Ukrainian resistance  Russia's Invasion wasn't going well  at the end of March after huge losses of  men and Machinery Russia abandoned its  attempt to seize Kiev  what they left behind shocked the world  butcher the most infamous but civilian  bodies were found in nearly every  settlement the Russians had occupied  often showing signs of torture and  execution  the seasons have carried Anastasia and  her grief through spring summer autumn  and now to Winter  when the Russians abducted her son it  didn't take him far just 200 meters down  the road to the pig farm where his body  was found  o I saw him being taken out which  there was a car outside they've taken  from one of the villagers when he  was the problem with this problem they  put him in and left I didn't know where  they were taken at half past five and  shot immediately that evening  as if he was sleeping  in the East the battle for Don Mass  became an attritional grind  but to the South Russia had more to show  for its efforts  on the as of Sea Coast finally fell to  the Russians in May a city of 400 000  people before the war lay in Ruins  but Ukraine Was preparing to strike back  it retook the kharkiv region in a  surprise September counter-offensive  that was followed by a strike on  Russia's bridge to Crimea and a forced  Russian Retreat from the city of her son  this was moscow's response running  shorts of military options Russia  launched drones and cruise missiles at  Ukraine's energy grid an attempt to  freeze the country into submission as  winter approached widespread blackouts  in Sub-Zero temperatures are a challenge  for everyone particularly those without  much money  dude Miller lives in a smoke blackened  bomb damaged apartment Block in here pin  yet she still counts herself lucky  to be honest my heart bleeds seeing  these ruins but we are alive we covered  the windows with film we had hope  because we have something left others  lost everything as 2022 ends ukrainians  leave behind them a year of  indescribable suffering but they take  with them a unity and a will to win  that's earned this country admiration  from around the world  there are still many people who doubt  that Ukraine can ultimately Prevail  against the might of Russia but few if  any of them come from this country ask  pretty much any Ukrainian what they  expect for 2023 and they only have one  answer Victory Rory Shannon's Al Jazeera  Kiev

